# Approval gates

Follow **AGENTS.md** section 4. Never answer an attestation, consent,
certification, signature or terms acceptance for the family. Show verbatim live
wording and every option before asking. Follow the Opt-in rule there.

## Do not create accounts or school profiles without asking

Any account creation, ARMS "Continue without one of these accounts", or step
that creates a school-side profile must be listed in the single approved
summary, naming the action and the disclosure the form shows. If it is not
listed, stop and ask. Inspect only public content until approved.

## Stop before ARMS Visitor Details / Verify Your Details

Treat **Visitor Details** and **Verify Your Details to Create a Profile** as
sending data to create a school profile. Stop before that step. Proceed only
if the summary the parent approved (full profile and final school list) lists
the profile creation, naming the action and its disclosure. In a dry run never
go past it unless data is fake and live-rehearsal disclosure is separately
approved. Never submit a dry run.

## Never click final Submit without family approval

After filling and immediately before **each Submit**, show the school, team,
final form URL, entered values, every preset choice and its confirmed final
answer, consent answers and file list. Ask a fresh school-specific question such
as: "Approve submitting this reviewed questionnaire to [school/team] at [URL]
now?" Wait for an explicit Yes. Approval for one school does not cover another,
a retry or a resubmission. Treat any action that sends a completed questionnaire
as Submit.

Before entering family data, get the parent's ONE approval ("Yes, fill these
forms") of the summary covering the full profile and the final school list with
each official form URL; never ask for separate profile and list approvals.
Record that Yes as BOTH `approvals.full_profile` and
`approvals.final_school_list` with the same quote and date but separate SHA-256
snapshot values. Small additions (non-sensitive extras only) go in the
per-Submit review without re-approval. ALWAYS re-ask a specific question about
just the item for a new or changed school, sport or team (or form link/type); any consent answer;
any file; any contact or phone number that could trigger SMS or AI-contact
authorization; and anything touching an ARMS profile not listed in the summary.
See CURSOR_PROMPT.md step 7; if wording differs, apply the stricter one.

For real-family runs: five groups -> one summary -> one Yes -> fill -> one
fresh Yes per Submit. The summary lists what will be entered into which
official form, including any specific ARMS profile-creation action. Do not add
a separate disclosure approval step, profile versions such as "v1" or "v2", or
whole-profile re-approvals. Separate live-rehearsal disclosure approval applies
only to deliberate dry-run tests on live forms, with fake data and no Submit.
Required consent, file, contact and other item-specific safety gates still apply.
